{"parentUuid":"b075e98a-fa27-42c6-a2a9-66665bed45f9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGatFyaSywrXu3oP14MU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed c0e6a461 on `hedgerow-grass` (not pushed): bullet hits now burst out of the surface instead of leaving round, pale puffs. I checked it headless only, on still frames and in `mv_burst.mp4` (sent above, a machine-gun burst raking a stone wall at exactly 60 fps), never in a real browser window.\n\n- **What I looked at:** this round was about the firefight itself. I captured a live exchange at the bridge with the AI shooting at a god-mode player, then fired controlled hits into stone, wood, steel and mud. Every hit left two round, pale dust balls hanging in the dark with no direction to them.\n- **What changed:** each hit now shoots two or three jets of dust and grit out of the hole, thrown on along the way the bullet glanced off. The air stops them within a third of a second, and a smaller, darker, ragged cloud is left to drift off. Stone, concrete and steel also flash white-hot for a frame or two. Hits on people are unchanged.\n- **How I compared:** I compared old and new code on five surfaces at 2 and 12 frames after each hit, plus the 60 fps burst. The new hits read as directional bursts that spread into ragged dust; mud stays subtle, as soft ground should. The steel and concrete targets were imperfect: the anti-tank gun registers as stone, and the bunker shot went into its firing slit.\n- **Not done:** enemy muzzle flashes at about 20 m last only two or three frames at roughly 10 pixels, so they're easy to miss. A minimum on-screen size for distant flashes is noted as a candidate for a later round.\n- **Checks:** all three quality presets compile with no errors, the nine node tests pass, and the branch still merges cleanly with hedgerow-poc.\n\nThe test server and headless Chrome are stopped, and the shared notes have this turn's details."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":276,"cache_read_input_tokens":700985,"output_tokens":621,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":276,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":621,"cache_read_input_tokens":700985,"cache_creation_input_tokens":276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":276},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9d118f68-e413-4331-a34e-943dd40d47f3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGatFLNnWYfTUrrZimp2","requestRef":"406845f7-9272-4369-b471-13f4224a9e94","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"130a0662-c805-468e-ad51-0d3ed8b5ba02","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:43:14.035Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
