{"parentUuid":"74857c16-61cd-443f-9dad-6becbada4916","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGbTys9gC7jVgMsvyGAT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014rdia9cTMjrEbajFNLpDAS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='fun/hedgerow/README.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    white-hot star in ragged orange tongues of burning gas, never the same\n    twice, a few grains of powder flung on ahead of it; a round's hit\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    white-hot star in ragged orange tongues of burning gas, never the same\n    twice, a few grains of powder flung on ahead of it, its star and\n    tongues never smaller on screen than 14 and 9 pixels across however\n    far off the gun is (bigger and a little dimmer, so a machine gun at\n    eighty metres still flickers as a flash, not a stray pixel); a round's hit\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"\"\"    cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, a muzzle's or a shell's flash\n    lighting the rain round it for its few frames (the player's own, at the\n    eye, hardly), none under a roof or an eave (the top of what is over\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, a muzzle's or a shell's flash\n    lighting the rain close round it faintly for its few frames, as faint\n    as the sliver of a frame a real flash lasts (the player's own, at the\n    eye, hardly), none under a roof or an eave (the top of what is over\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: distant muzzle flashes stay visible as flashes\n\nIn the live firefight an enemy MG at the far end of the bridge showed\nas a ball of lit rain around a flash only about 10 pixels across, for\ntwo or three frames. That is easy to lose and reads as a lamp, not a\ngun. In CoD and MoH night fights a distant gun is a sharp, flickering\nstar.\n\neffects.js: additive particles take an optional minimum on-screen size\n(`minPx`, carried in aMisc.w, which only lit particles used). A\nmuzzle's star and flame tongues never shrink below 14 and 9 pixels\nacross; past that they grow and dim by grow^-0.35, so a gun at 80 m\nstill flickers as a flash. Bullet strikes on stone and steel keep at\nleast 3 pixels. Measured on single flashes at 20, 40 and 80 m: the\nstar now holds its size at 40 and 80 m, where it was down to a few\npixels.\n\nweather.js: a flash lit the rain around it like a lamp, in a 2-4.5 m\nball, at full strength for its few frames, every shot. A real flash\nlasts about a millisecond, so flash-lit rain is now faint and close:\na 1.6 m box at 35% opacity with its brightness cap scaled to match,\nand the drops' lighting from flashes at 30%. The flash itself now\ncarries the shot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Update the README and commit the distant muzzle flashes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_read_input_tokens":518852,"output_tokens":1489,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":320},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":518852,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1196},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014rdia9cTMjrEbajFNLpDAS":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='fun/hedgerow/README.md'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    white-hot star in ragged orange tongues of burning gas, never the same\n    twice, a few grains of powder flung on ahead of it; a round's hit\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    white-hot star in ragged orange tongues of burning gas, never the same\n    twice, a few grains of powder flung on ahead of it, its star and\n    tongues never smaller on screen than 14 and 9 pixels across however\n    far off the gun is (bigger and a little dimmer, so a machine gun at\n    eighty metres still flickers as a flash, not a stray pixel); a round's hit\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"\"\"    cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, a muzzle's or a shell's flash\n    lighting the rain round it for its few frames (the player's own, at the\n    eye, hardly), none under a roof or an eave (the top of what is over\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    cap, rain falling through a fire's glow, a muzzle's or a shell's flash\n    lighting the rain close round it faintly for its few frames, as faint\n    as the sliver of a frame a real flash lasts (the player's own, at the\n    eye, hardly), none under a roof or an eave (the top of what is over\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: distant muzzle flashes stay visible as flashes\n\nIn the live firefight an enemy MG at the far end of the bridge showed\nas a ball of lit rain around a flash only about 10 pixels across, for\ntwo or three frames. That is easy to lose and reads as a lamp, not a\ngun. In CoD and MoH night fights a distant gun is a sharp, flickering\nstar.\n\neffects.js: additive particles take an optional minimum on-screen size\n(`minPx`, carried in aMisc.w, which only lit particles used). A\nmuzzle's star and flame tongues never shrink below 14 and 9 pixels\nacross; past that they grow and dim by grow^-0.35, so a gun at 80 m\nstill flickers as a flash. Bullet strikes on stone and steel keep at\nleast 3 pixels. Measured on single flashes at 20, 40 and 80 m: the\nstar now holds its size at 40 and 80 m, where it was down to a few\npixels.\n\nweather.js: a flash lit the rain around it like a lamp, in a 2-4.5 m\nball, at full strength for its few frames, every shot. A real flash\nlasts about a millisecond, so flash-lit rain is now faint and close:\na 1.6 m box at 35% opacity with its brightness cap scaled to match,\nand the drops' lighting from flashes at 30%. The flash itself now\ncarries the shot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Update the README and commit the distant muzzle flashes"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_014rdia9cTMjrEbajFNLpDAS":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"082fb418-7b7c-4bc2-85f5-e797cbd3d1be","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGbTyN8whHx36ptRtqNp","requestRef":"5b8e429d-1da9-4454-8ecb-9394c01523af","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"22796ab3-3ad1-4936-964f-16aaaac20c2f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T03:50:59.993Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
