{"parentUuid":"7242c07a-8932-4714-81ce-204f52ef459a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_012i9MA9xFZ1od16NnCNx4QH","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b764b0eb-ebf4-4db1-beac-d7139fa49608","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:08:17.271Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"b764b0eb-ebf4-4db1-beac-d7139fa49608","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGcnuVNMaujQXs2gsztH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LEunpZDCw5J2DGAdQfxrR5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/assets/textures/mud.webp fun/hedgerow/assets/textures/mud_n.webp fun/hedgerow/tools/textures.py && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the mud is churned, so strong light breaks up on it\n\nUnder a flare ahead, the wet mud of the lane and the forest track lit up\nas an even silvery glaze with its brown lost, like frost. The mud\ntexture claimed to be \"churned\", but its height was dominated by\n4 m-scale swells: its normal map came out almost flat (slopes ~3-4\ndegrees) and its gloss varied only at that large scale. Under a strong\nlight ahead, a smooth glossy sheet is what you get.\n\ntools/textures.py mud(): the height now carries churned relief: lumps a\nfoot across (spectral lo=10) and smaller ones squeezed up between them\n(lo=30), with the clods rounded off by the wet instead of reading as\ndried cracks. The normals come from that relief (strength 16: tilt sd\n0.21, between the forest floor and the cobbles). The gloss follows where\nthe water lies: hollows relative to the mud around them at two scales\n(4 cm and 16 cm, so it still breaks up far off under mipmapping),\ncrests drained and dull. The albedo palette is unchanged.\n\nA/B'd in place (old and new textures swapped in the running page) on\nthe lane under a live flare: glints on the lumps with brown between them\ninstead of the glaze. At night with no flare the two are identical (the\nsame mean to the decimal). mud_n.webp grows from 353 KB to 1.2 MB, near\nthe grass and forest normal maps.\n\nFound on the way: in a forest, ground more than 40 m from the player is\noutside the flare's shadow map, so it gets no canopy shadow. Not changed\nhere.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the churned mud texture"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":638164,"output_tokens":792,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":638164,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LEunpZDCw5J2DGAdQfxrR5":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/assets/textures/mud.webp fun/hedgerow/assets/textures/mud_n.webp fun/hedgerow/tools/textures.py && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the mud is churned, so strong light breaks up on it\n\nUnder a flare ahead, the wet mud of the lane and the forest track lit up\nas an even silvery glaze with its brown lost, like frost. The mud\ntexture claimed to be \"churned\", but its height was dominated by\n4 m-scale swells: its normal map came out almost flat (slopes ~3-4\ndegrees) and its gloss varied only at that large scale. Under a strong\nlight ahead, a smooth glossy sheet is what you get.\n\ntools/textures.py mud(): the height now carries churned relief: lumps a\nfoot across (spectral lo=10) and smaller ones squeezed up between them\n(lo=30), with the clods rounded off by the wet instead of reading as\ndried cracks. The normals come from that relief (strength 16: tilt sd\n0.21, between the forest floor and the cobbles). The gloss follows where\nthe water lies: hollows relative to the mud around them at two scales\n(4 cm and 16 cm, so it still breaks up far off under mipmapping),\ncrests drained and dull. The albedo palette is unchanged.\n\nA/B'd in place (old and new textures swapped in the running page) on\nthe lane under a live flare: glints on the lumps with brown between them\ninstead of the glaze. At night with no flare the two are identical (the\nsame mean to the decimal). mud_n.webp grows from 353 KB to 1.2 MB, near\nthe grass and forest normal maps.\n\nFound on the way: in a forest, ground more than 40 m from the player is\noutside the flare's shadow map, so it gets no canopy shadow. Not changed\nhere.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the churned mud texture"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01LEunpZDCw5J2DGAdQfxrR5":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c2525e14-c42d-4e79-a116-86171e5fd648","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGcntSsJ4pWzBk4vNLuV","requestRef":"95bae8bf-f4ab-4695-b151-fbd6c958e519","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2fdd7513-2283-4939-8f63-e570be58f8a4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:08:17.270Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
