{"parentUuid":"72dd9408-4ead-4b0e-83cf-7ac8cbaa86a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGcod99SwF8jyMuXssNS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PMRZBVSTQ3kksoXWCZeBTa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n\nTurn of 2026-10-22, fourteenth:\n- Chased a \"snowy\" flare-lit floor. Findings (keep): (1) freezing G.flares.update and then moving\n  the camera leaves the flare's shadow map (ortho +-40 m round where the camera was) behind - test\n  views get NO canopy shadows; my chg_flare/fd_* frames of the last rounds were that artifact.\n  Use flare_live.js (flare running, relaunch until one is ahead) or pin the light (flare_fixed.js:\n  sun.position/target set per view, sun.shadow.needsUpdate each frame). (2) In real play ground\n  > 40 m from the player is outside that shadow map -> no canopy shadow -> pale patches far down\n  the forest track under a flare. Candidate: a top-down canopy cover map for the far field.\n  (3) The flare's specular cut on its own: FILL_UNIFORMS (fill.js) uFillDir[1] = flare dir and\n  uFillSpec 0 from scene.onBeforeRender. (4) Debug a terrain term: wrap the terrain material's\n  onBeforeCompile, append `gl_FragColor = vec4(<expr>, 1)` after dithering_fragment, new cache key.\n- 9a3721b4 the mud is churned: textures.py mud() height + churn (lo 10) + lumps (lo 30) + blurred\n  clods (no dried cracks), normal strength 16 (tilt sd 0.21 vs 0.05 before), gloss = 0.62 +\n  4(h - blur12) + 3(h - blur40) - 0.15 ruts + 0.1(h - .5). mud_n 353 KB -> 1.2 MB. A/B in place\n  (mud_swap.js: old webp as data URLs swapped into the terrain's tMud/tMudN uniforms): under a\n  live flare glints on lumps instead of a glaze; at night with no flare identical.\n  Checks: low/high compile, 9 node checks, merge-tree clean. Not seen in a real browser window.\nEOF\nREDACTED; cd $S && node hl.mjs stop; rm -rf hl-profile; p