{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"020dc1a195adee8ecc257295bc5dd3990669936e6fdc4efb6b95fc2bdc98b3a8","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QGgNXk2RjuU3EBm6abQL8D","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/js/weather.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: night rain shows by the light it catches\n\nThe far rain sheets drew every streak in the same grey whatever lit it,\nso at night the dark sky was covered in evenly bright streaks like\nstatic. Real night rain is hardly visible in the dark and glitters near\nlamps (RealRain/HQ-NightRain photographs, arXiv 2510.17440).\n\nEach sheet streak now shows by the light it catches: a faint veil out in\nthe dark, stronger near a lamp, a fire, a flare or in lightning. Near and\nfar drops catch lamplight through a forward-scattering lobe\n(Henyey-Greenstein, g 0.45), so rain seen against a lamp is brighter than\nrain lit from the side or from behind the eye.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the night-rain visibility change"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
