{"parentUuid":"29d6751b-7f43-4116-9be1-34c32b0bee7d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGwBE5n2EouM4shDV6p5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rebased `hedgerow-grass` onto `main` as you asked, then committed ac5ee8d4: the forest canopy now shades the floor under a flare. Nothing is pushed, and I checked it all headless only, never in a real browser window.\n\n**Rebase**\n- `hedgerow-poc` is gone; it was merged into `main` and deleted. I rebased onto `main` at 4dab1486 (\"the head bob keeps time with the feet\"). That's 42 commits replayed with no conflicts, and the result is exactly the old branch plus that one new commit.\n- The fetch failed because the sandbox has no access to your SSH key, so I rebased onto `main` as it was last fetched. If anything newer is on the remote, it isn't included.\n- `origin/hedgerow-grass` still points at the old pre-rebase history (9a3721b4). Bringing it in line needs a `git push --force-with-lease`, which I haven't done.\n\n**Forest floor under flares**\n- **The cause:** the flare's shadows only cover the area around the player, and low quality draws no flare shadows at all. So on low, the whole forest floor took a pale, snow-like sheen under every flare.\n- **What changed:** at load, `canopy.js` maps the tree crowns from above. Wherever the flare's shadows don't reach, the ground dims the flare's light by how much canopy is over it. The wet track still glints where the crowns open over it.\n- **Result on low** (image above): the forest floor drops to about half its brightness (22→12 and 20→10.5 in two track views).\n- **Result on high:** the shadows already reach about 62 m toward the flare and 40 m to the sides, and the dense forest hides most ground further out. So the change only shows on long sightlines, and in my test views high looked the same before and after.\n- **Correction to last round:** the extreme \"snow\" frames I reported came from my own test method, not the game. With the flare running normally, the far pale patches on high are real light through the gap in the trees over the track.\n- **Checks:** all three quality presets compile with no errors, the nine node tests pass, and the branch merges cleanly with `main`.\n\nThe test server and headless Chrome are stopped, and the shared notes have the rebase details and this round."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":715492,"output_tokens":733,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":253,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":733,"cache_read_input_tokens":715492,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":253},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5a4a31ab-fcef-40f6-a1a3-99282cacd2a4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGwBDHPr78bTXy3H8B54","requestRef":"ec3c16ef-a515-44a8-990f-1ce6cafcb1ac","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"c3a6dfcd-e134-4d5c-8234-e7f2604b16e8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:09:22.483Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-grass","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
