{"parentUuid":"fd6f4d43-0956-46a6-8c39-8df9f20cd770","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGwaVGU4psnrzmyqBbJA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011PVWQirtaRFUyw3GehYvTh","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    metal (now and then off mud) skips on, slower, often up into the sky;\n    tracers and sparks never","new_string":"    metal (now and then off mud) skips on, slower, often up into the sky;\n    a tracer its compound burning white-hot in a line drawn out by its\n    speed, in a soft orange-red glow, brightest at its head (never under\n    three pixels there, so one far off is still a point of fire on its\n    line); tracers and sparks never"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":742311,"output_tokens":951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":951,"cache_read_input_tokens":742311,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011PVWQirtaRFUyw3GehYvTh":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    metal (now and then off mud) skips on, slower, often up into the sky;\n    tracers and sparks never","new_string":"    metal (now and then off mud) skips on, slower, often up into the sky;\n    a tracer its compound burning white-hot in a line drawn out by its\n    speed, in a soft orange-red glow, brightest at its head (never under\n    three pixels there, so one far off is still a point of fire on its\n    line); tracers and sparks never"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"aeb3a1ce-48ed-420c-bfa4-72ae0a3b4b88","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGwaUQPJRUGG6j2okdDz","requestRef":"b4ea0874-48a8-4b07-8357-ea1f4cfedaca","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"37beeb77-a18b-4ff6-bdf3-666d065e6186","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:14:33.623Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-grass","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"37beeb77-a18b-4ff6-bdf3-666d065e6186","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGwaVGU4psnrzmyqBbJA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DdAtEkFw1m7XpwvVCs7E38","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: tracers burn, with a glow and a hot head\n\nA tracer was one thin pale-yellow streak (4.5 cm, never under 1.5 px).\nCrossing the dark lane it read as a scratch on the picture, and incoming\nas a faint dash. In CoD and MoH night fights a tracer is a burning line:\na white-hot core in a soft orange-red glow, brightest at its head.\n\neffects.tracer() now spawns three particles flying together:\n- the core: a white-hot streak (#ffe8c8 x3.2, cooling towards the\n  caller's colour), drawn out a little further by its speed (streak\n  0.012 -> 0.016);\n- a glow streak around it: 20 cm wide, dim, orange-red (#ff5a1e, a\n  0.5);\n- the head: a bright spark-cell point at the front of the streak, never\n  under 3 px on screen (the minimum size added for muzzle flashes), so\n  a tracer far off is still a point of fire on its line.\n\nA/B'd on the dark lane at an exact 60 fps (stepped page clock): crossing\nat 25 m and 60 m, and incoming from 45 m. The player's own tracer leaves\nthe muzzle fast enough that its glow is already several metres out in\nthe first frame, so there's no glare at the eye. Three particles per\ntracer instead of one, in a pool of 2,500.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the burning tracers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":742311,"output_tokens":951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":951,"cache_read_input_tokens":742311,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DdAtEkFw1m7XpwvVCs7E38":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git add fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: tracers burn, with a glow and a hot head\n\nA tracer was one thin pale-yellow streak (4.5 cm, never under 1.5 px).\nCrossing the dark lane it read as a scratch on the picture, and incoming\nas a faint dash. In CoD and MoH night fights a tracer is a burning line:\na white-hot core in a soft orange-red glow, brightest at its head.\n\neffects.tracer() now spawns three particles flying together:\n- the core: a white-hot streak (#ffe8c8 x3.2, cooling towards the\n  caller's colour), drawn out a little further by its speed (streak\n  0.012 -> 0.016);\n- a glow streak around it: 20 cm wide, dim, orange-red (#ff5a1e, a\n  0.5);\n- the head: a bright spark-cell point at the front of the streak, never\n  under 3 px on screen (the minimum size added for muzzle flashes), so\n  a tracer far off is still a point of fire on its line.\n\nA/B'd on the dark lane at an exact 60 fps (stepped page clock): crossing\nat 25 m and 60 m, and incoming from 45 m. The player's own tracer leaves\nthe muzzle fast enough that its glow is already several metres out in\nthe first frame, so there's no glare at the eye. Three particles per\ntracer instead of one, in a pool of 2,500.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","desc