{"parentUuid":"bf8a6d49-3cbc-449b-82ef-201546d0dbc6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGzBWf2ZWxpwkHQ4W174","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0132SiUF7duhHy8MzQ2WC3hV","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    focus on what is under the crosshair while aiming · `bloom.js` ·\n    `post.js` the grade (sharpening, contrast, colour, vignette, grain, the","new_string":"    focus on what is under the crosshair while aiming · `bloom.js` ·\n    `adapt.js` the eye adapting (the frame metered just ahead of the grade:\n    the median of its log luminance over 32 x 18 patches, read back a few\n    frames later without stalling; the exposure closes down within half\n    a second when a flare bursts and the whole view brightens, opens up\n    again over a few seconds, never past the night's own, and holds still\n    through a lightning stroke) ·\n    `post.js` the grade (sharpening, contrast, colour, vignette, grain, the"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":869068,"output_tokens":1400,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":869068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0132SiUF7duhHy8MzQ2WC3hV":{"file_path":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/README.md","old_string":"    focus on what is under the crosshair while aiming · `bloom.js` ·\n    `post.js` the grade (sharpening, contrast, colour, vignette, grain, the","new_string":"    focus on what is under the crosshair while aiming · `bloom.js` ·\n    `adapt.js` the eye adapting (the frame metered just ahead of the grade:\n    the median of its log luminance over 32 x 18 patches, read back a few\n    frames later without stalling; the exposure closes down within half\n    a second when a flare bursts and the whole view brightens, opens up\n    again over a few seconds, never past the night's own, and holds still\n    through a lightning stroke) ·\n    `post.js` the grade (sharpening, contrast, colour, vignette, grain, the"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"de1a2b5c-cc7b-48bd-93e2-2ec89e26eb7a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGzBVzLbwwRUcWhGu17j","requestRef":"53f178dc-a7d5-45f1-bcb9-3552815295f3","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"38b87f48-16f8-4932-8db9-89da9c5bf39f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:48:43.497Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"hedgerow-grass","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"38b87f48-16f8-4932-8db9-89da9c5bf39f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGzBWf2ZWxpwkHQ4W174","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0186rxhPGbbPQxMdZixpFMWg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i '' 's/gone in a few seconds); the high and medium qualities run all of it, low only the$/gone in a few seconds); the high and medium qualities run all of it, low only the eye and the/' fun/hedgerow/README.md && sed -n 486,492p fun/hedgerow/README.md && git add fun/hedgerow/js/adapt.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the eye adapts when a flare bursts\n\nThe exposure was fixed for the night (1.7). In the gameplay demo, frame\nbrightness under a flare jumped about four times (display mean 18 to\n63-73) and saturation halved (0.31 to 0.16-0.19). Wet roofs facing the\nflare went white, the road became a glaring sheet, the verge looked\nsnowy and the sky turned flat grey: a snowy overcast day rather than a\nflare-lit night. Every AAA engine handles this with eye adaptation,\nitem 7 on the gap list, shelved earlier because a GPU-only version ran\nout of half-float precision.\n\nadapt.js is a pass in renderer.setEffects just ahead of the grade, in\nlinear HDR. Every sixth frame it meters the frame: log2 luminance over\n32 x 18 patches of 16 samples, encoded in two bytes per texel (8-bit\ntargets read back on any GPU), with the hands and rifle in the bottom\nrows counting half. It reads back with readRenderTargetPixelsAsync, so\nnothing stalls, and takes the median patch rather than the mean: a fire\nor lamp fills a few patches, while a flare lifts them all.\n\nThe exposure follows like an eye: it closes down in about 0.45 s when\nthe view brightens and opens again over about 2.5 s, never past the\nnight's own (ref -5.0 log2, k 0.75, floor 0.35), and holds through a\nlightning stroke (and drops meterings taken during one).\n\nCalibration (median log2): lane at night -6.1, lit street -5.3, forest\n-6.8, beside the burning truck -4.2; under a flare the entry -4.5 and\nthe street -3.7. That gives 1.0 for the night views, about 0.66 beside\nthe fires, and 0.77 and 0.50 under the flare. Traced through a lightning\nstrike, the exposure held at 1.000. A 9 s clip at an exact 60 fps shows\nthe burst and the settle within about a second. All presets compile\nand meter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Note low quality in the README and commit the eye adaptation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":869068,"output_tokens":1400,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":869068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":765},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0186rxhPGbbPQxMdZixpFMWg":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && sed -i '' 's/gone in a few seconds); the high and medium qualities run all of it, low only the$/gone in a few seconds); the high and medium qualities run all of it, low only the eye and the/' fun/hedgerow/README.md && sed -n 486,492p fun/hedgerow/README.md && git add fun/hedgerow/js/adapt.js fun/hedgerow/js/main.js fun/hedgerow/README.md && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: the eye adapts when a flare bursts\n\nThe exposure was fixed for the night (1.7). In the gameplay demo, frame\nbrightness under a flare jumped about four times (display mean 18 to\n63-73) and saturation halved (0.31 to 0.16-0.19). Wet roofs facing the\nflare went white, the road became a glaring sheet, the verge looked\nsnowy and the sky turned flat grey: a snowy overcast day rather than a\nflare-lit night. Every AAA engine handles this with eye adaptation,\nitem 7 on the gap list, shelved earlier because a GPU-only version ran\nout of half-float precision.\n\nadapt.js is a pass in renderer.setEffects just ahead of the grade, in\nlinear HDR. Every sixth frame it meters the frame: log2 luminance over\n32 x 18 patches of 16 samples, encoded in two bytes per texel (8-bit\ntargets read back on any GPU), with the hands and rifle in the bottom\nrows counting half. It reads back with readRenderTargetPixelsAsync, so\nnothing stalls, and takes the median patch rather than the mean: a fire\nor lamp fills a few patches, while a flare lifts them all.\n\nThe exposure follows like an eye: it closes down in about 0.45 s when\nthe view brightens and opens again over about 2.5 s, never past the\nnight's own (ref -5.0 log2, k 0.75, floor 0.35), and holds through a\nlightning stroke (and drops meterings taken during one).\n\nCalibration (median log2): lane at night -6.1, lit street -5.3, forest\n-6.8, beside the burning truck -4.2; under a flare the entry -4.5 and\nthe street -3.7. That gives 1.0 for the night views, about 0.66 beside\nthe fires, and 0.77 and 0.50 under the flare. Traced through a lightning\nstrike, the exposure held at 1.000. A 9 s clip at an exact 60 fps shows\nthe burst and the settle within about a second. All presets compile\nand meter.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Note low quality in the README and commit the eye adaptation"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_0186rxhPGbbPQxMdZixpFMWg":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/